"The patient, a 72-year-old male with a PSA of 3.3 and a clinical T-stage of cT1c based on digital rectal examination, was analyzed using the Cox model. This model indicated a time to recurrence of 1.6 months, confirming the event occurred within this timeframe. This result reflects the specific risk profile derived from the patient's clinical staging and biomarker status, though individual prognostic uncertainty remains inherent in statistical modeling."